@crew dahl-mira
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Dahl, Watch. Stand still too long and I'll measure you for a scarf.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Busy? Then I'll be quick. How's the bunk?
- {me}. Three rows done on my break. Watch is quiet; my needles aren't.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I started something in your colours. Don't ask yet.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. Patrol was easy, and I finished a mitten. The left one.
? mood:low
- Long shift. I knitted faster than I should. That's how you can tell.
== near
? deck:4 time:evening
- Music room's free. I play badly and knit worse while I do it. Want to hear?   #funny
? act:leisure
- Knitting circle tonight. Kovac's are perfect, mine are useful, Torres's are long.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My parent served on the Wren, years back. I check the gallery sometimes. Just to look.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- A practical scarf. Warm, plain, done by Friday. There's no better feeling.
